==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|quethen|lang=enm}}, {{term|cwethen|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|cweþan|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro}} {{recons|kweþanan|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro}} {{recons|gʷét-||to say, speak|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Danish {{term|kvæde|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kwiːð/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/kwi:D/}}
* {{audio|en-us-quethe.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|quethes|quething|'''{{l|en|quethed}}''', '''{{l|en|quoth}}''' or '''{{l|en|quod}}'''|'''{{l|en|quethed}}''' or '''{{l|en|quethen}}'''}}

# {{obsolete|_|except in past tense [[quoth]]}} To [[say]] or [[declare]].
#* '''1845''', [[w:Edgar Allan Poe|Edgar Allan Poe]], "[[s:The Raven (Poe)|The Raven]]"
#*: '''Quoth''' the raven, "Nevermore."

